{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963828-elysium-on-a-boat-miami-an-80s-requiem","id":963828,"title":"Elysium on a boat (Miami an 80s Requiem)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T12:04:01-07:00","id":963828,"title":"Elysium on a boat (Miami an 80s Requiem)","content":"One of my player is going to be starting an internship in a hospital soon with 12 hours shift followed by homeworks. So as we only have a session per month she said she didnt mind continuing playing but she would like for the 2 next session to be more light. I had planned for the next session to be set in the elysium and i would like ideas for small stuff that would happen in an elysium so that she can be entertained but would not need to be too focused.<br /> <br /> Setting:<br /> <br /> As i stated in the title it is in miami in the 80s and the players are going at the elysium hosted by the primogen of the invictus on his boat. I had planned for the elysium to be about first formally introducing the characters to the All-Night Society (don't know why but i love that term) and also as a platform for the mighty to discuss the worrying events happening in the town lately with the big finally being a murder happening on the boat followed possibly by a fire. I'd rather wait for my player to have finished her internship before reaching that last part.<br /> <br /> Namely hunters are on the rise and seem to have eeringly accurate knowledge of where vampires would be and Kindred are noticing that the network they control are being influenced, subverted or outright destroyed (mostly criminal networks) by an unknown entity or organisation that the Kindred are starting to call Lasombra (no relation to the VtM clan). <br /> I myself have not yet decided who or what it will be.<br /> <br /> Recap:<br /> <br /> So do you guys have any idea what little events i could give my players for the next 2 sessions that would be entertaining but would not require to much concentration? The point is that i would continue with the whole murder and fire after the players internship.<br /> <br /> Also i don't want to bloat my post so tell me if it would be useful to know more about the setting (whats the state of the covenants in the setting and theyre leader and so forth) or about the PCs and i'll right another post going more into detail.<br /> <br /> Thank you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:32:16-07:00","id":963844,"title":"","content":"We had a lot of fun with an auction. Strange artifacts, prestigious or rare objects, blood dolls with the Producer Merit, a 'favor' from an enigmatic vampire, the Prince always auctioned off an allowed Embrace. For some offerings 'substitutions' could be made in place of money. There's a lot you could do with it, offering up plot hooks to the characters and even if a purchase isn't made there's always negotiations or plotting that can be done afterwards.<br /> <br /> If you're using the Aegis Kai Doru it can be tied in with motive for them to seek the boat out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T12:57:37-07:00","id":964483,"title":"","content":"Nice idea. I wanted to give my PCs the opportunity to buy a nightclub and the auction would fit nicely with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:03:18-07:00","id":967167,"title":"","content":"It's Miami in the 80's, have the local kindred and especially their little meetings on a boat draw a federal drug investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:46:31-07:00","id":967304,"title":"","content":"I take you have New Wave Requiem, so I will just say a couple things<br /> <br /> One thing from the book that I think would be interesting would be to have a gaggle of neonates arguing that the 80s vampires obsession in popular culture means the masquerade is no longer needed, the book says that was a surprisingly popular position in the 80s, and there are just as many elder who think the 80s vampire media represents a collapse of the masquerade, an argument between the two could be a good event.<br /> <br /> Also, inspired by something that happened to my parents when they lived in Miami in the 80s, have a wealthy elder mention how their favorite expensive car was stolen and offer a big reward to whoever finds it. Let the PCs actually think it might be an easy payday, then keep them from finding the car for a while, often by just missing it, and implying that the car is being used for something interesting and illegal. Do this long enough for it to be a brick joke when they finally find the car in flames on the side of the interstate while on an unrelated adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:51:00-07:00","id":967997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963828-elysium-on-a-boat-miami-an-80s-requiem?p=967304#post967304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing from the book that I think would be interesting would be to have a gaggle of neonates arguing that the 80s vampires obsession in popular culture means the masquerade is no longer needed, the book says that was a surprisingly popular position in the 80s, and there are just as many elder who think the 80s vampire media represents a collapse of the masquerade, an argument between the two could be a good event.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a very interesting idea. I was searching for a way to give a distinct feel to the carthians in the domain and i think that idea is a good way to approach that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:54:19-07:00","id":967998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963828-elysium-on-a-boat-miami-an-80s-requiem?p=967167#post967167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Miami in the 80's, have the local kindred and especially their little meetings on a boat draw a federal drug investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely plan on having the feds starts unwittingly circling the kindred community. <br /> <br /> Also, i thought of having elysium end with a kindred and a few ghouls murdered (with no suspect found) followed closely by a surprise arrival of a federal drug investigation team. Tho that team will get mindwiped fairly easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:31:32-07:00","id":968961,"title":"","content":"&quot;80s Miami VtR&quot;<br /> <br /> This is VERY MUCH MY THING. <br /> <br /> Here's a weird true thing that happened in Miami during that period: reptile smuggling. Reptile smuggling was a huge business. The same gangs that ran cocaine carried snakes, turtles, frogs, and lizards from literally all around the world, and Miami was their playground. The books &quot;The Lizard King&quot; and &quot;Stolen World&quot; are both about this, and it's really the kind of fascinating weirdness that would work great in ChroD. <br /> <br /> For example, maybe the vampires want these rare and dangerous snakes and crocodiles to make them into ghouls? Maybe the Circle wants them for various rituals or potions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-14-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:35:39-07:00","id":969336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963828-elysium-on-a-boat-miami-an-80s-requiem?p=968961#post968961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;80s Miami VtR&quot;<br /> <br /> This is VERY MUCH MY THING.<br /> <br /> Here's a weird true thing that happened in Miami during that period: reptile smuggling. Reptile smuggling was a huge business. The same gangs that ran cocaine carried snakes, turtles, frogs, and lizards from literally all around the world, and Miami was their playground. The books &quot;The Lizard King&quot; and &quot;Stolen World&quot; are both about this, and it's really the kind of fascinating bit of weird that would work great in ChroD.<br /> <br /> For example, maybe the vampires want these rare and dangerous snakes and crocodiles to make them into ghouls? Maybe the Circle wants them for various rituals or potions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very interesting. I think i'll introduce that idea to my player by having them see that owning a reptile (ghoul or not) is the new ''fashion'' in elysium. Maybe even pattern each harpy with a different type of reptile???<br /> One thing for sure, i want to use that idea somewhere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thx.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:54:22-07:00","id":969351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/963828-elysium-on-a-boat-miami-an-80s-requiem?p=969336#post969336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Very interesting. I think i'll introduce that idea to my player by having them see that owning a reptile (ghoul or not) is the new ''fashion'' in elysium. Maybe even pattern each harpy with a different type of reptile???<br /> One thing for sure, i want to use that idea somewhere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thx.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you liked it! I'd definitely recommend The Lizard King if you're looking for an interesting read. And I do believe there's a Bloodline in Requiem with snek powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}